# Provenance and modification notice

This repository is self-contained: it vendors the openpi codebase so that
readers do not need a separate openpi checkout.

## Vendored upstream code

- **Upstream project:** [Physical-Intelligence/openpi](https://github.com/Physical-Intelligence/openpi)
- **Base commit:** `981483dca0fd9acba698fea00aa6e52d56a66c58`
- **License:** Apache-2.0 (see `LICENSE`; Copyright (c) Physical Intelligence)

Vendored from the base commit (unmodified unless listed below):

- `src/` — the openpi Python package
- `packages/` — the `openpi-client` workspace package
- `scripts/` — training / serving entry points
- `examples/libero/` — LIBERO eval client used by `eval/`
- `pyproject.toml`, `uv.lock`

The Gemma / PaliGemma model weights are **not** distributed in this
repository. They are subject to the separate terms in
`LICENSE_GEMMA.txt` and must be downloaded separately (see the README).

## Files modified by this project (Apache-2.0 section 4.3)

The method of the paper (Let It Be Simple, arXiv:2606.05737) lives
directly in the source tree. The following five upstream files are
modified relative to the base commit:

1. `src/openpi/models/model.py` — adds the `PI0_SCD` / `PI0_A2A` /
   `PI0_RAE` model-type enum values, a `state_history` observation
   field (A2A), and relaxed image/image-mask shape annotations for
   video inputs.
2. `src/openpi/models/pi0.py` — adds the high-noise time-shift
   schedule (`noise_shift_alpha`), the SimVLA action head
   (`cond_head_mode="simvla"`), learned action-start controls, and
   frequency-weighted loss paths.
3. `src/openpi/models/pi0_config.py` — adds the configuration knobs for
   the above: `noise_shift_alpha`, `time_sampling`, `cond_head_mode`,
   and the `simvla_*` head parameters.
4. `src/openpi/policies/policy_config.py` — threads
   `data_config.quantile_norm_keys` into the `Normalize` / `Unnormalize`
   transforms (eval-server path).
5. `src/openpi/serving/websocket_policy_server.py` — serving-side
   additions for the eval server.

## Additional files taken from the authors' openpi development branch

The five modifications above depend on code that does not exist in the
base commit. The following files are taken verbatim from the authors'
development branch of openpi (the same branch the modifications were
developed on):

- `src/openpi/models/simvla_head.py` (new) — SimVLA transformer action head
- `src/openpi/models/action_patchifier.py` (new) — action patchifier used by the model/config
- `src/openpi/models/perceiver_resampler.py` (new) — perceiver resampler used by the SimVLA head
- `src/openpi/models/vjepa.py` (new) — V-JEPA vision encoder support
- `src/openpi/training/weight_loaders.py` (modified) — adds
  `TruncatedPaliGemmaWeightLoader`, `Pi0FromPaliGemmaWeightLoader`,
  `SelectiveTruncationWeightLoader`, and a configurable `missing_regex`
- `src/openpi/transforms.py` (modified) — adds `quantile_keys` support
  to `Normalize` / `Unnormalize`
- `scripts/train.py` (modified) — applies `backbone_lr_multiplier`
  gradient scaling, robust checkpoint restore, and offline LeRobot
  version-check handling

## Minimal integration edits

- `src/openpi/training/config.py` — (a) registers the paper configs:
  `import openpi.training.misc.paper_configs as paper_configs` and
  `*paper_configs.get_paper_configs()` in `_CONFIGS`; (b) adds the
  `quantile_norm_keys` field on `DataConfig` and the
  `backbone_lr_multiplier` field on `TrainConfig`, both verbatim from
  the development branch, required by the files above.

## Files original to this repository

- `src/openpi/training/misc/paper_configs.py` — the paper's 25 run configs
- `src/openpi/training/misc/CONFIG_NAMES.txt` — the released config names
- `experiments/`, `diagnostics/`, `eval/` — theory validations,
  diagnostic protocols, and the LIBERO evaluation harness
- `experiments/pi0-endpoint-geometry/` — 11 analysis helper modules written for
  this paper (endpoint/episode sigma-1 probes, dense sheet tracking,
  commit-mechanism and causal scans). Their checkpoint roots read `LBS_CKPT_ROOT`;
  the result JSONs they produce are not part of this release
